WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:03.210
Jerry and Galamon needed to be saved and fast!

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:06.050
So the Tamers used the red card Shibumi made for them,

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:08.750
and the final battle against the De-Reaper was on!

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.930
Meanwhile, the Monster Makers frantically put the finishing touches

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.130
on their plan to delete the big blob!

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.680
Then Jerry took action,

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.060
but that just added fuel to the De-Reaper's fire!

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.280
This giant thing rose out of nowhere,

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.360
and it looked like Galamon was done for!

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.440
But Grani came to the rescue and gave his last remaining strength

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.900
so Galamon could digivolve in crimson mode!

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.000
Aw, man! This is it, guys!

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.380
I can't believe we're flying!

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.660
Thanks to Grani, we'll get there in no time!

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.270
Hold on, Jerry, we're coming!

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.890
Kalamon, come over here, quick!

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:46.490
Oh, you don't have a choice!

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:49.160
I'm through sitting around!

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:50.150
It's time!

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.460
Time I did something more than just cry!

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.750
We're gonna have our hands full here!

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:58.610
I hope Zakuya-mon, Mega-gargo-mon, and Jeski-mon are doing okay!

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:30.000
idea cybertramon ready come on listen to me i want

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.590
I want you to send all your power to my blade!

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:33.590
Quickly!

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:35.800
What? You can't be serious!

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.860
To your head or something, the force of it could kill the both of you!

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:44.560
It's a chance I'm willing to take, Rika. We've tried everything else and we haven't even landed a scratch!

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:51.140
But with the combined forces of your strength and our blade, we could give the D-Reaper something to really howl about!

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.890
Or you could die! Did you ever think about that, Hotshot?

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:58.960
Well, then there'll be just one less person to poke fun at you, right, Pumpkin?

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:03.790
You big twerp, you're just doing this to impress me, aren't you?

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:06.410
So, is it working or not?

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:10.440
Come on, Sakuya-mon! It's now or never!

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.930
Rika, you sure?

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:16.000
Ryo may be out of his pompous mind, but he's also right.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.240
It's the only chance we have of destroying that thing!

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.760
*Gasps*

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:30.000
My body, my soul, my mind, I now send to you.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:41.330
the strength within my heart my spirit to you I now really give

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:09.350
everything he can he knows we can't play it safe anymore

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:41.720
The power to change our lives lies in ourselves!

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.810
See, it worked! I told you'd be a piece of cake, didn't I?

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.660
Well, if anyone could do it...

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.210
It's you, Ryo.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.890
Good luck!

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.540
Rika, are you alright?

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:25.540
I guess that took more out of us than I thought.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.150
Come on, no chance!

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:10.000
Digimon exists only to destroy or be destroyed, an exercise of futility.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.830
You have to be kidding me!

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:16.770
Humans desire total annihilation, therefore their existence is pointless.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:19.970
No! You don't get to decide that!

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:25.450
My life isn't pointless and neither is Geomon's or my friends or anyone else's!

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:30.000
We have a right to live and to protect the people we care about!

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.330
Looks like you could never understand.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.510
Ah!

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:44.960
The other side!

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:51.340
I'm detecting a massive wormhole in the heart of the de-reaper bubble.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:54.800
Alright, engage Operation Doodlebug.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.650
Doodlebug launch in T-minus ten seconds.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:59.860
Booting systems now!

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:02.040
Tal, are you sure that this is safe?

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:04.630
Well, are we ready?

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.830
I guess we're as ready as we'll ever be, Dolphin.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:14.840
Work, Daisy.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:16.050
It has to.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:17.630
Look at the line.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:18.650
Isn't it pretty?

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:21.080
Where'd you go?

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:24.310
We've been in tighter spots, right, Calamon?

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.750
We'll escape or someone will rescue us.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:30.000
I hope.

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:42.140
It's an open communication line.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:44.520
Right, this is it.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:45.520
Henry, Terriormon!

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:48.040
Come in, can you hear me?

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:49.040
Is that you, Dad?

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:51.120
Henry, listen to me.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:55.190
I've loaded a program inside of Terriormon.

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:57.190
My ear feels really funny.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:58.140
So that's what it was.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.060
Hold it!

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.440
I'm sorry, I should have told you.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.490
Henry, it's the Juggernaut Program.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:08.100
Juggernaut?

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:12.420
Why did you put it inside a Terriormon?

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:16.870
Juggernaut was designed to work like a small-scale Big Bang.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:21.870
The program creates an intense energy vortex that sucks in all digital life forms.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.880
And nothing can escape it.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:25.880
Why would you activate it now?

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:30.000
Henry, look below you. It's a wormhole connecting the real world to the digital dimension.

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:37.550
It transfers D-Reaper's data faster than the speed of light.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:39.780
That's how it evolves and grows so rapidly.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:44.630
By using Juggernaut, we can reverse the process by sending D-Reaper back where it came from

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.740
and devolving it into a harmless program.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:50.390
That's just what we've been looking for! You guys are amazing!

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:57.360
We've made the necessary modifications to Juggernaut, so it won't harm you or any of your friends.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.730
You just tell me what to do!

